# Environment
# .env is tracked on purpose: it holds only public values (project URL, the
# publishable/anon key, project id) that ship to the browser anyway, and the
# deploy reads it. Every OTHER env file is ignored, so a real secret
# (service_role, LOVABLE_API_KEY, any sb_secret_*) can never be committed by
# accident. Server secrets belong in the deployment environment, never here.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vercel build output (Nitro emits this when VERCEL is set)
.vercel
